<surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Cade</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Underreporting of energy intake in four populations of African origin</article-title><source>Int J Obes Relat Metab Disord</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>882</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10918535</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21-vhrm-4-1115"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mirmiran</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Azadbakht</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohammadi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1382</year><article-title>Correlation of under and over reporting of energy intake to BMI and lifestyle related factors: Tehran Lipid and Glucose study (TLGS)</article-title><source>Journal of Iran University of Medical Sciences</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>22</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b22-vhrm-4-1115"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pryer</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Vrijheid</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nichols</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Who are the &#x02018;low energy reporters&#x02019; in the dietary and nutritional survey of British adults?</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>146</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9126514</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23-vhrm-4-1115"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Samaras</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelly</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Campbell</surname><given-names>LV</given-names></name></per